        "original_id": "92be4e99-f5f9-5126-bc05-297d02b7fcfa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Downton, Herefordshire, Downton-on-the-Rock\n- Historical Records: Domesday Book, Great Survey\n- Concepts: civil parish, place-name meaning\n\nFacts:\n- Downton is a civil parish in Herefordshire in the north of the county.\n- Downton contains the village of Downton-on-the-Rock.\n- The Domesday Book was the \"Great Survey\" of much of England and parts of Wales completed in 1086.\n- In the Domesday Book, Downton is referred to as \"Herefordshire Council.\"\n- The name given for Downton is stated to mean \"hill settlement.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
