        "original_id": "0218d668-4b26-58aa-9734-f034b9c3ced1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Downton, Herefordshire\n- Works: Domesday Book\n- People: William the Conqueror\n- Concepts: place names, Great Survey\n\nFacts:\n- In 1086, the Domesday Book was completed as a manuscript record of the Great Survey of much of England and parts of Wales by order of William the Conqueror.\n- The Domesday Book is also known in Latin as Liber de Wintonia, meaning Book of Winchester.\n- In the Domesday Book, Downton in Herefordshire is referred to as \"Duntune.\"\n- The name \"Duntune\" means \"hill settlement.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
